.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Playwright / harness toolchain, installed locally, not part of the product.
# package.json is ignored deliberately: `npm init -y` writes the git remote URL
# into it, and this repo's remote carries a PAT. GitHub push protection blocked
# exactly that push once already. Recreate the toolchain with:
#   npm install playwright && npx playwright install chromium --with-deps
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json

# Python bytecode — never ship this inside the pack
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Render evidence: the A/B arms the owner must look at are committed.
# The four control-repeat images are NOT — they were proved pixel-identical to
# A_baseline (pairwise MSE exactly 0), so committing ~42 MB of duplicates adds
# nothing. Their value is in metrics_control.json, which IS committed.
results/ws4/A2_control_repeat/*.png
results/ws4/A3_control_repeat/*.png
results/ws4/A4_control_repeat/*.png
results/ws4/B2_no_vae_roundtrip_repeat/*.png

# R3: the crop-factor control arm's PNG is byte-identical (max abs diff 0 over
# 2688x3456x3) to results/face/arms/C_zface_steps_08/HasMetadata_00016_.png,
# which is already committed. It was a server-health control, not a new result.
# Its api_graph.json and meta.json ARE committed.
results/r3_crop/R3_control_cf3/*.png

# R1: the two control-repeat PNGs are proved identical (mean abs diff 0.0000,
# max 0) to results/face/arms/L1b_steps08_loras/HasMetadata_00031_.png, so
# committing 22 MB of duplicates adds nothing. The numbers are in meta.json.
results/face/control/R1_control_L1b_repeat/*.png

# TRACK A (results/crash/A): ~20 arms x 2 PNGs x 11 MB = 200 MB+ of 2688x3456
# frames. The full-resolution originals stay on the pod under
# results/crash/A/arms/. What IS committed instead:
#   * results/crash/A/A4_contact_sheet.png  -- the two A4 panels at 1:1, full res
#   * results/crash/A/thumbs/*.png          -- the 621:163 face region of EVERY
#     arm, cropped to the detector's own box and halved, so the whole ladder is
#     inspectable from the repo
#   * every api_graph.json, meta.json and /history JSON, uncompressed
# The detector numbers that the argument actually rests on are in
# results/crash/A/arm_yolo.json and yolo_A4.json, not in the pixels.
results/crash/A/arms/*/*.png

# TRACK V band sweep (results/crash/V/arms/V_SW_*): 25+ ladder arms at ~14 MB of
# PNG each. Their evidence is the status/error node in meta.json and the measured
# black/blob/YOLO figures in results/crash/V/out/v_checks.json, all of which ARE
# committed. The pixels add ~400 MB and nothing a reader needs. Same reasoning as
# the ws4 control repeats above.
results/crash/V/arms/V_SW_*/*.png

# Oversized artifacts (GitHub hard-blocks files over 100 MB; no LFS by
# decision). These live only on the pod. History of personal-max was
# rewritten on 2026-08-08 to drop every version of them. sha256 of the
# pod copies at rewrite time, so a re-fetch or re-cut can be verified:
#   f8cdfc791a8cea4416c5d0f741ed052deef075e604aab7c0f0e52ae7e0270dcd  Personal-NSFW/loras/luna.safetensors      (162 MB, re-downloadable; hash-verified at REF-PREFLIGHT a74525f)
#   47deda1b4886b334fa1ab84e2a056c13c0c24acb90339767097f9a5b5f50f003  Personal-NSFW/loras/lunaskye.safetensors  (177 MB, re-downloadable; hash-verified at REF-PREFLIGHT a74525f)
#   f70c9af4425333abf3998fb2051dc3f681a743e4e348066bb10e65f4624833d7  dist-personal/AIOFMTech-NSFW-Personal.tar.gz  (276 MB, pack v3 f70c9af4 — the hash the run-5/6 reports cite; re-cuttable from this repo + the two LoRAs)
Personal-NSFW/loras/*.safetensors
dist-personal/*.tar.gz
